{% comment %}
  Scoped styling for the desktop mega menu (the subjects menu, 8 L1 / 31 L2 / 126 L3).

  Rendered from snippets/gazelle-layout.liquid, NOT from sections/header.liquid —
  header.liquid is a Horizon core file and must not be edited. gazelle-layout is
  already render-hooked in theme.liquid, so this adds no new core-file touch.

  ⚠️ MOST OF THE MEGA MENU IS NATIVE. Read this before adding anything here.
  blocks/_header-menu.liquid drives BOTH levels entirely from CSS variables
  (--menu-parent-font-* / --menu-child-font-*), derived in
  snippets/submenu-font-styles.liquid from three block settings:

    type_font_primary_link  font family/weight/style for BOTH levels (shared)
    type_case_primary_link  uppercase or none, for BOTH levels (shared)
    menu_font_style         the size + colour PRESET pair, three options:

      regular        parent = md size, full foreground   | child = sm size, subdued
      inverse        parent = sm size, SUBDUED           | child = md size, full   <- Horizon default
      inverse_large  parent = sm size, subdued           | child = xl size, full

  "Column headings heavier than their links" is therefore a SETTING, not CSS:
  menu_font_style must be 'regular'. The default 'inverse' does the exact
  opposite — headings smaller and greyed, links larger and darker.

  What genuinely is NOT available natively, and so lives here:
    1. font-weight differing between parent and child. Both read the same
       --font-<preset>--weight token, so no setting can separate them.
    2. a distinct treatment for the trailing "All <parent>" link.
    3. the panel's own background / border.

  The "All X" hook: those items carry no distinguishing class — mega-menu-list.liquid
  emits every third-level link as a plain .mega-menu__link. But build_gazelle_menu.py
  always appends "All <parent>" as the LAST item of each column's list, so
  li:last-child is a reliable structural hook and NO label change is needed.
  (The brief's fallback of prefixing labels with "→ " was not used — a CSS hook
  beats editing 20 menu labels.)

  ⚠️ .mega-menu__link--parent is applied only when a link HAS children
  (mega-menu-list.liquid:112). The 4 merch items under "Gifts & stationery" and the
  7 links under "Trade & publishers" have none, so they render as plain
  .mega-menu__link and will NOT pick up the heading treatment. That is arguably
  correct — they are links, not column headings — but those two panels will read
  differently from the six subject panels.
{% endcomment %}

{%- comment -%}
  HEADING VARIANT TOGGLE (section 1 of the visual-pass brief).
  Change this one value and re-push to screenshot the other option:
    'a'  Cinzel 15px / 500 / 0.02em tracking / #000 / no uppercase   <- default
    'b'  Switzer 600 15px  (the previous treatment)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign heading_variant = 'a' -%}

{% style %}
  /* ---------- 1. Mega panel: column headings ---------- */
  .mega-menu__link--parent {
    {% if heading_variant == 'b' %}
      font-family: var(--font-body--family);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 15px;
      letter-spacing: normal;
    {% else %}
      font-family: var(--font-heading--family);
      font-weight: 500;
      font-size: 15px;
      letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    {% endif %}
    text-transform: none;
    color: #000;
    margin-block-end: 10px;
  }

  /* ---------- 2. Third-level links ---------- */
  .mega-menu__list .mega-menu__link:not(.mega-menu__link--parent) {
    font-family: var(--font-body--family);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: #000;
    text-decoration: none;
    /* .mega-menu__link carries padding-block: var(--padding-2xs); 3px a side
       gives the 6px between links the brief asks for. */
    padding-block: 3px;
  }

  .mega-menu__list .mega-menu__link:not(.mega-menu__link--parent):hover {
    color: #940000;          /* accent, matches scheme-1 primary */
    text-decoration: none;   /* colour shift only, no underline */
  }

  /* ---------- 3. The trailing "All <parent>" link ---------- */
  /* Always the last item of a column's child list, so :last-child is exact and
     no label in build_gazelle_menu.py needs an arrow baked into it. */
  .mega-menu__list ul > li:last-child > .mega-menu__link {
    font-family: var(--font-body--family);
    font-size: 14px;
    color: rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / var(--opacity-subdued-text));
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }

  .mega-menu__list ul > li:last-child > .mega-menu__link::after {
    content: ' \2192';       /* U+2192 RIGHTWARDS ARROW, inherits the muted colour */
  }

  .mega-menu__list ul > li:last-child > .mega-menu__link:hover {
    color: #940000;
  }

  /* ---------- 4. Panel sheet ---------- */
  /* White, to sit flush with the header rather than reading as a separate
     card. Hairline top edge, no shadow - the Waterstones "calm sheet". */
  .mega-menu {
    background-color: #fff;
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--color-border, #e8e2d8);
    box-shadow: none;
    padding-block: 28px;
  }

  /* ---------- 5. Panel width ---------- */
  /* The panel div carries `section section--full-width-margin section--page-width`
     and core's `.section--page-width > * { grid-column: 2 }` should already centre
     it, but it renders full-bleed. Pin it to the same token the rest of the site
     uses so the menu shares the 1200px rail. */
  .mega-menu .mega-menu__grid {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: var(--page-content-width);
    margin-inline: auto;
    --menu-horizontal-gap: 32px;
  }

  /* ---------- 6. Column sizing ---------- */
  /* mega-menu-list.liquid hardcodes --menu-columns-desktop: 6 for every text
     panel, so a panel was always six equal tracks however many columns it holds.
     auto-fit collapses the empty tracks. The max is 1fr, NOT a px ceiling: an
     earlier fixed 224px ceiling assumed a 1200px container and crushed the fifth
     column when the container was narrower. 200px is a hard floor, so a column
     that will not fit WRAPS to a second row instead of being crushed.
     At 32px gaps: 5 x 200 + 4 x 32 = 1128, inside 1200. */
  @media screen and (min-width: 990px) {
    .mega-menu .mega-menu__grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
    }

    /* A lone column would otherwise take the whole 1fr track and run the full
       width of the grid. :only-child cannot match a multi-column panel. */
    .mega-menu .mega-menu__grid > .mega-menu__column:only-child {
      max-width: 260px;
    }
  }

  /* ---------- 7. Header bar (section 2) ---------- */
  /* 15px is NOT available natively: type_font_primary_size offers 0.625 / 0.75 /
     0.875 / 1 / 1.125rem only, so 0.9375rem has to come from CSS. Set the token
     rather than font-size so anything else keyed to it follows. */
  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .menu-list {
      --menu-top-level-font-size-desktop: 0.9375rem;
    }
  }

  /* Underline on hover AND while the panel is open. [aria-expanded='true'] is
     Horizon's open-state hook (blocks/_header-menu.liquid:394 gates the submenu
     on it). inset box-shadow rather than border-bottom so nothing shifts by 2px.
     NOTE: no "boxed outline" exists in the theme CSS - see the report. */
  .menu-list__link:hover,
  .menu-list__link[aria-expanded='true'] {
    box-shadow: inset 0 -2px 0 0 #940000;
  }

  /* ---------- 8. Mobile drawer (section 3) ---------- */
  /* The drawer is a different template (snippets/header-drawer.liquid) and does
     not use .mega-menu__* at all, so the "All X" treatment has to be repeated
     here. Third-level items reuse --child, so the last --child in a list is the
     "All X" row. */
  .menu-drawer__menu-item--child:last-child .menu-drawer__menu-item-text {
    color: rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / var(--opacity-subdued-text));
  }

  .menu-drawer__menu-item--child:last-child .menu-drawer__menu-item-text::after {
    content: ' \2192';
  }
{% endstyle %}
